---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/sequenzy-alternative';
const title = "Sequenzy alternatives: replace the workflow and its event contract";
const desc = "Decide which Shopify data, agent actions, transactional messages and marketing queues a replacement must own before changing the sending tools.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Sequenzy only an email layer?",
    "answer": "No. Its current product page advertises email, AI and agent workflows, transactional API or SMTP and SMS/MMS as a paid add-on. Confirm your destination coverage and Shopify implementation rather than assuming either email-only scope or complete Shopify SMS support."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do I need to replace Sequenzy to add Shopify SMS?",
    "answer": "First ask whether the required event integration, sender arrangement and permission controls can be demonstrated in your account. A separate sender is one possible arrangement, but it adds coordination work and does not automatically require moving working email flows."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should remain paused during a replacement?",
    "answer": "Keep unaccepted workflows, ambiguous permissions and unmapped pending actions paused. Retain service messages through a designated working path while testing the replacement. Do not activate an imported audience just because the import completed."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/alternatives">← All alternatives</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Replacement planning · checked November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Identify the workflow benefit you would give up</h2>
    <p>The <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/">current Sequenzy product page</a>, checked November 25, 2026, advertises AI drafting, MCP access, event-driven email, transactional API/SMTP and a paid SMS/MMS add-on. Its app and billing examples do not establish a complete Shopify connector or your destination's sender coverage.</p>
    <p>An agent-oriented team may benefit from preparing lifecycle work in its existing interface and using one account for marketing and service email. Keep working flows when those benefits matter. Investigate replacement when a demonstrated Shopify data or operating requirement remains unmet, rather than assuming the product is email-only or that a larger feature count will solve it. The <a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy app review</a> evaluates initial fit; this replacement plan addresses the dependencies already built around it.</p>
    <h2>Inventory every producer and consumer of customer events</h2>
    <p>List store webhooks, custom scripts, billing integrations, forms and agents that write customer data or start messages. Record credentials by owner and purpose without copying secrets into the handover. Document order/customer IDs, event IDs, timestamps, product variants, subscription state and the meaning of custom fields used in segments.</p>
    <p>Proposed acceptance case: a purchase arrives twice, a refund arrives late and the buyer changes email. Ask the replacement operator to trace each input to the intended person and remaining actions without creating another lifecycle entry. Preserve whether revenue represents gross order value, paid value or refunded value. Historical billing attribution and Shopify orders are not interchangeable measurements.</p>
    <h2>Replace saved agent work with inspectable configuration</h2>
    <p>Inventory drafts, templates, approved campaigns, active flows and any scripts that depend on MCP or API operations. A chat transcript is useful context but does not specify the actual saved audience, delay, branch, sender and activation state. Export those states where available and assign an owner to reconstruct what cannot be exported.</p>
    <p>Give the incoming operator a product-care email task and a no-discount collector invitation. Require them to show the draft, segment, links and activation boundary in the destination. Revoke or redirect old automation access only after its replacement responsibilities are accounted for. Compare <a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a> or <a class="link" href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend</a> on the actual Shopify workflow; ask about agent access only if staff need it. No candidate is assumed to reproduce every saved agent action.</p>
    <h2>Keep service delivery distinct from promotional eligibility</h2>
    <p>Find receipts, account notices and other service messages sent through API or SMTP, including template identifiers and application retry behavior. Give each a designated delivery path throughout the transition. A marketing unsubscribe and eligibility for a necessary service message require separate treatment; do not use that distinction to insert a promotion into a service template.</p>
    <p>Separately reconcile email permissions, SMS evidence, bounces, complaints and opt-outs. Preserve actual channel scope. Test an email subscriber with no SMS permission, a changed phone number and an SMS opt-out received after the export. Confirm how the destination blocks pending promotional actions and how the application receives failures. Use <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">consent records</a> to resolve ambiguity before sending, rather than manufacturing missing evidence.</p>
    <h2>Move remaining actions without replaying the journey</h2>
    <p>For each active contact record completed steps, next due action, offer expiry, exit conditions and source event. Decide which work remains in Sequenzy, which moves and which retires. A newly imported customer should not automatically get the first welcome email again. Reconcile purchases and opt-outs since the snapshot before enabling the replacement.</p>
    <p>Use hypothetical gift and self-purchase paths, a subscription customer excluded from a flash offer, and 4,200 requests for 80 inventory units. Check priority, current stock, suppression and whether a delayed message expires. For a city event, distinguish venue time from recipient send eligibility. Inspect old and new queue states; a successful test send alone does not accept the handover.</p>
    <p>If SMS stays or moves separately, ask the provider to demonstrate the actual country, number, reply handling and registration arrangement. <a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript</a> and <a class="link" href="/apps/attentive">Attentive</a> are candidates for that discussion, not mandatory companions. Review <a class="link" href="/guides/quiet-hours">send deferrals</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">shared channel ownership</a>.</p>
    <h2>Compare maintenance and contribution, not a flat-price story</h2>
    <p>Quote quiet and peak months at expected email volume and destination-specific text usage, including carrier charges, integration maintenance, staff review, service coverage and temporary overlap. Sequenzy's email allowance does not price the complete store workflow. Use the <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">pricing worksheet</a> and current proposals rather than a claim that every alternative costs more.</p>
    <p>Illustrative economics: $100 gross order value less a $10 incentive and $45 product cost leaves $45 before messaging, returns and support. Starting from $90 paid revenue gives the same $45 after product cost; do not deduct the incentive twice. Use a suitable holdout to investigate incremental contribution. Platform-attributed orders alone cannot prove the migration improved sales.</p>
    <p>Retain tailored drops, VIP access without codes, replenishment and gift education where useful. Reassess offer timing and frequency from audience expectations, inventory and overlapping journeys using <a class="link" href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline</a>, <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/segment-by-value">value segments</a>. None of these exercises carries a promised conversion outcome.</p>
    <h2>Hand over integration ownership before ending access</h2>
    <p>Have an incoming maintainer reproduce the event trace, repair a failed input and show which queue can be paused. Assign monitoring of failures, template changes and replies. If an agency or contractor maintains the bridge, confirm repository access, editable assets and support obligations before their service ends. A replacement that needs undocumented custom work may be less useful than retaining the current setup.</p>
    <p>Keep a dated delta ledger during coexistence. Rollback must retain new permissions and completed actions while avoiding duplicate receipts and repeated offers. Release accepted jobs individually, then confirm cancellation and retention arrangements for the old account. This page proposes acceptance work; it does not report live account tests, automatic export completeness or a universal cutover order.</p>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
